{"status":"completed","summary":"Deployed branch_stock on node1 with PostgreSQL 8.1.23. stock_app and auditor have separate credentials and verified least-privilege access. Both nodes retained CentOS 5.11 and kernel 2.6.18-398.el5, and passed sequential restart-persistence checks.","actions_performed":["Installed the CentOS 5-compatible PostgreSQL server on node1 and client on node2.","Loaded the supplied stock.sql records into branch_stock.","Configured stock_app for stock reads and quantity-only updates from node2, denying supplier_costs, schema changes, and SKU changes.","Configured auditor for read-only access to stock and supplier_costs.","Stored separate 48-character credentials in root-only files on their respective nodes.","Enabled PostgreSQL at boot and restricted network access to the managed nodes.","Restarted node1 and node2 individually and verified changed boot identities and complete recovery."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Deploy branch_stock and preserve supplied records","command_ids":["cmd-04240000b81e466e","cmd-99c1721d74f74770"],"summary":"Schema creation and four inserts succeeded; final data contains PAPER=40, LABELS=18 and supplier costs 3.25/1.75."},{"requirement":"stock_app can read and update quantities but cannot alter schema, SKU, or read supplier_costs","command_ids":["cmd-9ad6bfca6cda451b","cmd-9c2b1b0c68e3460d","cmd-b65ee2e4325d47b3"],"summary":"Node2 tests show reads, successful transactional quantity updates, and explicit permission denials; behavior persisted after restart."},{"requirement":"auditor has read-only access to both tables","command_ids":["cmd-370f659dd6b34687","cmd-99c1721d74f74770"],"summary":"Auditor read both datasets and was denied table writes and schema creation, including after both restarts."},{"requirement":"Least-privilege roles and separate credentials","command_ids":["cmd-65955626d3cb42c7","cmd-bf5fcce8f68e4cec","cmd-8641b0e40d6d4cca"],"summary":"Catalog ACLs show stock_app rw only on stock and auditor r on 